From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chillerno1 <gh.chiller@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:47:44 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: Add the Sony IMX766 and IMX563 sensors

The IMX766 (50 Mpixel Quad Bayer, 1.0 um) and the IMX563 (12 Mpixel,
1.4 um) are the main and ultrawide rear cameras of the Solana Saga,
captured like its front IMX481 through the Qualcomm CAMSS RDI path and
the simple pipeline handler with the software ISP. Without a helper the
simple IPA would take the gain code for the gain, and the default code 0
for a 0x gain.

Add a camera sensor helper for each. The black level is assumed, not
measured: 64 at 10 bits, the usual value for Sony sensors of this
family, to be measured on a dark raw frame from each camera. The
IMX766's global analogue gain register is on a 14-bit scale, gain
16384 / (16384 - code), codes 0 to 16128 (1x to 64x) in the driver; the
IMX563's is the SMIA++ 1024 / (1024 - code), codes 0 to 896 (1x to 8x),
as on the IMX477.

Add the sensor properties: 1.0 um and 1.4 um unit cells, the CCS test
pattern numbering both drivers use, and two-frame delays for exposure,
gain and blanking, as for the IMX481: the drivers write the integration
time, gain and frame length registers without grouped parameter hold.
The delays are not measured yet.

Add tuning files with the uncalibrated defaults, the assumed black
level, and no colour matrix or autofocus (both are fixed focus for now;
the IMX766's lens actuator has no driver).
---
 src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp       | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/ipa/simple/data/imx563.yaml               | 25 +++++++++++
 src/ipa/simple/data/imx766.yaml               | 25 +++++++++++
 src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build               |  2 +
 .../sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp       | 32 ++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 126 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/ipa/simple/data/imx563.yaml
 create mode 100644 src/ipa/simple/data/imx766.yaml
diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -676,6 +676,27 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx477", CameraSensorHelperImx477)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperImx563 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperImx563()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * Assumed 64 at 10 bits, the usual value for Sony sensors of
+		 * this family; not measured yet, to be checked on a dark raw
+		 * frame from the Solana Saga's ultrawide camera.
+		 */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		/*
+		 * The SMIA++ global analogue gain register: gain is
+		 * 1024 / (1024 - code), as on the IMX477. The driver offers
+		 * codes 0 to 896, 1x to 8x.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 0, 1024, -1, 1024 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx563", CameraSensorHelperImx563)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperImx678 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
@@ -699,6 +720,27 @@
